    {
      "topic_id": "bearings_angle_facts_F",
      "prompt": "The bearing of W from U is 067°. The lines pointing north at U and at W are parallel. Using co-interior angles, find the bearing of U from W.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "North at U and north at W are parallel lines, and UW is a straight line crossing both (a transversal) - so the angle between the transversal and north on one side of it at one point, and the angle between the transversal and north on the *same* side at the other point, are co-interior angles: they sum to 180°.",
        "The bearing of W from U is 067°, so the co-interior angle at W (between north at W and WU) = 180° - 67 = 113°.",
        "The bearing of U from W is measured the rest of the way round from north, clockwise, past that co-interior angle: 180° + 67° = 247°."
      ],
      "final_answer": "247°",
      "marks": 4,
      "mark_scheme": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
